          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 6.4: Let us spread awareness"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.126,
            0.745,
            0.203
          ],
          "content": "Work in groups to **design** posters and pamphlets about various aspects of responsible social media behaviour and paste them at designated places in the school. Also, fill in Table 6.4 based on your collective observations."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.24,
            0.786,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "| Dos | Don'ts |\n| --- | --- |\n| Be respectful and kind. | Do not share personal photos with strangers/ virtual friends. |\n| Think before posting. | ___________________ |\n| Protect privacy. | ___________________ |",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.126,
                0.212,
                0.682,
                0.233
              ],
              "content": "Table 6.4: Dos and don’ts to be followed on social media"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_10_table_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.42,
            0.743,
            0.466
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "6.4.5 Avoiding harmful substances — learn to say NO"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.473,
            0.744,
            0.584
          ],
          "content": "Some people, including your peers, may tempt, persuade, force or, create pressure on you to consume harmful substances such as tobacco, gutka, cigarettes, beedi, alcohol, or even life-threatening illegal drugs. Since adolescence is marked by curiosity and excitement, adolescents might get influenced by such people and try these substances."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.585,
            0.744,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": "These substances are not just harmful to physical and mental health but are also addictive. This means that once people start consuming them, they develop a strong urge to take them again and again. Over time, they start using them regularly. This is called **substance abuse**."
        },
        {
